From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a page drags on the desk

Dragging text, an image or a link out of a page did nothing on a tty. Ozone
DRM and headless windows have no `WmDragHandler`, and
`DesktopDragDropClientOzone::StartDragAndDrop` answers a drag with no
handler with kNone before it starts. Nothing logged it.

`DesktopWindowTreeHostPlatform::CreateDragDropClient` now gives such a
window the desk's own handler, `DeskDragHandler`
(ui/views/widget/desktop_aura/domicile/desk_drag_handler.h), as ash runs
its own drags:

- An `aura::Env` pre-target handler takes every event while the drag runs,
  in the root window's DIPs, and hands moves and the release to the
  window's drop handler, which is the client itself.
- Escape or a touch cancel cancels.
- The drag image is a layer at the top of the root window.

The client finds a drop's target with `aura::DeskWindowAt`, so a drop on
another monitor of the desk reaches the desk page, as an event there does.

Every platform with a window manager keeps its own handler.

`DeskDragTest` covers the drag's steps. `test-a-page-drags-on-the-desk.sh`
reads the series for the wiring.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
